    #!/bin/sh
    # Milestone 1 part 5 P2 run.log (specs/0012-styles.md, "P2" and "Harness
    # runs"): the corpus run on both targets with --tool-arg --style-sample,
    # using the debug binaries gate.log built and hashed, the run log's own
    # comparison of the input and output parts, and the record pair.
    #
    # P2's acceptance, from "Harness runs", lo and lo_in ok in every case:
    #  - in every workbook the styles part and the first worksheet part
    #    `changed`, every other entry `identical` unflagged, `descriptor` alone
    #    allowed on a changed entry, `order_preserved` yes, `files_identical` no;
    #  - the run log's own check over the extracted input and output parts: the
    #    three byte spans of the styles part identical, the input's children a
    #    prefix of the output's in both containers, one numFmt added with the
    #    expected id and `count` grown by one, two xfs added (the first carrying
    #    that id and applyNumberFormat, the second exactly the bytes "Harness
    #    runs" gives) and `count` grown by two; for the worksheet, `changed` equal to
    #    `styled` with A's `s` alone different, one cell added at (M + 1, 1) with
    #    `s` equal to X + 1, and nothing removed;
    #  - `read_back` equal to `styled + 2` in every file;
    #  - totals `xfs_after` 1046 and `formats_added` 27.
    #
    # WRITTEN FOR M1 part 5 P2 from P1's run script (records/logs/m1p5-p1/
    # run.log). What differs from that one, and why:
    #  1. The operation is --style-sample, which edits: the outputs are NOT the
    #     input's bytes, and two entries per workbook change. P1's checks for a
    #     byte-identical output and for every entry identical are replaced by
    #     the classification P2's acceptance states, with the two changed rows
    #     matched against the part names the comparison picks (the names are
    #     read, never printed).
    #  2. The comparison is P2's (cmp.py, printed below). It reads each archive
    #     with zipfile and expat, sharing no code with the library or the tool,
    #     makes its own pick of A, M, X and F from the INPUT, and then compares
    #     the input and output parts by bytes and by cell. It raises seventeen
    #     flags, and --plant <flag> plants a difference for each one: the
    #     control this log runs for every flag it trusts.
    #  3. A plant that cannot falsify its flag on a given pair says so
    #     (planted=no) rather than passing for want of a difference; the control
    #     accepts a flag that stayed yes only when the plant reports that.
    #  4. The comparison's own controls run on three generated pairs, built here
    #     and edited by the host debug binary: a sheet with a styled number, a
    #     sheet with no sampled cell, and a styles part with no numFmts of its
    #     own (the created-container case of P1 verification ruling 5).
    #  5. The two count flags hold the OUTPUT's count attribute to the output's
    #     own children, and those children to one (numFmts) or two (cellXfs)
    #     more than the input's, because that is what the library writes: it
    #     counts the children it has and adds its additions, never trusting the
    #     input's attribute. Whether the input's own attribute agreed with its
    #     children is a property of the corpus file, so it is reported beside
    #     the flags (fmt_count_in_matched, xf_count_in_matched) instead of
    #     being folded into them, where a corpus file with a stale count would
    #     have raised a false failure.
    #  6. P2 has no size record. The status check accounts for this phase's
    #     logs, its record pair and one planning file: specs/0012-styles.md,
    #     modified and uncommitted at the hash planning gave for its "Planning
    #     rulings during P2" (ruling 8 keeps it out of P2's commits).
    #
    # ATTEMPT 3, after independent check 1 and planning's "Planning rulings
    # during P2" in specs/0012 (2026-09-22). What changed from attempt 2, and why:
    #  A. The script is printed into the log in full, under "## script", as P1's
    #     run log did (ruling 1). Attempts 1 and 2 printed the comparison and
    #     the generator but not this script.
    #  B. dated_xf_ok is byte equality with the string "Harness runs" gives for
    #     the second added xf, no longer six attribute substrings (ruling 2).
    #     A second plant, dated_xf_order, writes the same attributes and values
    #     in another order; on every control pair and on the first corpus pair
    #     it must turn dated_xf_ok to no and leave every other flag yes.
    #  C. The comparison reads with expat, not ElementTree. Both are independent
    #     of the library, and expat gives the byte offsets the span check needs;
    #     specs/0012's "ElementTree" in "P2" and "Harness runs" is read as "an
    #     independent Python XML reader" (ruling 4).
    #  D. Every verdict other than as-expected is counted, and the end of the
    #     log prints the count and how many of them read UNEXPECTED (ruling 6).
    #  E. The status check accounts for the uncommitted spec by its hash
    #     (item 6 above).
    #  The corpus run itself, the runner, the record script, the binaries and
    #  every other check are attempt 2's. The record pair is written again under
    #  the same stem; attempt 2's pair was moved aside first and is hashed below
    #  with the superseded attempts.
    #
    # None of the three shapes specs/0001 forbids appears here: every compound
    # condition is a named function and every negated one goes through isnot,
    # whose control is below; the shapes are described rather than written out.
    #
    # Workbooks appear as ids only. No original name, note, producer_version or
    # app, and no corpus path: the corpus directory is written <corpus>. The
    # comparison prints counts and yes/no flags only: no reference, no value, no
    # text, no format code, no part name.
    #
    # Usage: m1p5-p2-run.sh <phase commit> > <scratch file>; the caller moves the
    # output to records/logs/m1p5-p2/run.log. One runner pass per target over 27
    # workbooks with a LibreOffice conversion each, so the caller starts it
    # detached and polls.
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    . scripts/counting.sh
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    export RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never
    CORPUS=${EMEND_CORPUS_DIR:-$HOME/emend-testing}
    LO_IMAGE=localhost/emend-lo:25.2.3-2-deb13u6
    SHORT=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)
    DATE=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)
    # A rerun takes a run directory of its own, RUN_TAG naming it (the runner
    # refuses a second row for an id in one directory).
    RUN_TAG=${RUN_TAG:-}
    RUN=$DATE-$SHORT$RUN_TAG
    OUT=$CORPUS/runs/$RUN
    STEM=m1p5-p2-$DATE-$SHORT
    HEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    EDIT=--style-sample
    fail=0
    
    # note <what> <verdict>: one verdict line, and a verdict other than
    # as-expected fails the log.
    # Every verdict other than as-expected is counted, and UNEXPECTED on its own,
    # so the log's end can print both counts (P2 ruling 6).
    nbad=0; nunexp=0
    note() {
      echo "  $1: $2"
      if [ "$2" != as-expected ]; then
        fail=1; nbad=$((nbad + 1))
        [ "$2" = UNEXPECTED ] && nunexp=$((nunexp + 1))
      fi
    }
    # is <command...>: as-expected when the command succeeds.
    is() { if "$@"; then echo as-expected; else echo UNEXPECTED; fi; }
    # isnot <command...>: as-expected when it fails, so no call hands a negation
    # to `is`, which specs/0001 forbids as a shape.
    isnot() { if "$@"; then echo UNEXPECTED; else echo as-expected; fi; }
    hide() { sed "s#$CORPUS#<corpus>#g; s#$MAIN#<repo>#g; s#$HOME#<home>#g"; }
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    W=$(mktemp -d) || exit 2
    trap 'rm -rf "$W"' EXIT INT TERM HUP
    
    nrows() { awk -F'\t' 'NR > 1 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # columns_resolve <tsv> <names>: every named column is in the file's header,
    # and there is a header at all.
    columns_resolve() {
      awk -F'\t' -v want="$2" '
        NR == 1 {
          seen = 1
          for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) have[$i] = 1
          n = split(want, w, " ")
          for (j = 1; j <= n; j++) if (!(w[j] in have)) miss++
          exit
        }
        END { exit (seen != 1 || miss > 0) }' "$1"
    }
    count_where() {
      awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" -v v="$3" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next }
        k && $k == v { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    sum_col() {
      awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next }
        k { n += $k } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    # kv <line> <key>: the value of key=value in a line whose pairs are split on
    # tabs or spaces; empty when the key is absent.
    kv() { printf '%s\n' "$1" | tr '\t ' '\n\n' | sed -n "s/^$2=//p" | head -1; }
    # kvn <line> <key>: the same, 0 when absent or not a number, for totals; a
    # workbook whose line is short is refused by accept_one, so a 0 here cannot
    # hide it.
    kvn() {
      local v
      v=$(kv "$1" "$2")
      case "$v" in '' | *[!0-9]*) echo 0 ;; *) echo "$v" ;; esac
    }
    
    # The guard, before a line of the run exists.
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    is_head() { full_sha "$1" && [ "$1" = "$HEAD_SHA" ]; }
    if ! is_head "$C"; then echo "the phase commit must be HEAD as a full sha, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "about: M1 part 5 P2 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $HEAD_SHA"
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $HEAD_SHA"
    note "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(is full_sha "$C")"
    note "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(is is_head "$C")"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" "$(isnot is_head "$NULL_SHA")"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" \
      "$(isnot is_head "$(printf '%s' "$C" | cut -c1-7)")"
    note "control: isnot reports a passing command as UNEXPECTED, so it can fail" \
      "$(is [ "$(isnot true)" = UNEXPECTED ])"
    echo "phase: Milestone 1 part 5 P2 (specs/0012-styles.md) run.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" \
            "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time\n' "$(basename "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then
        echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"
      fi
    fi
    echo "SERIALIZED: produced with no other run in flight"
    echo "DETACHED: no interactive call waits on this run; stdout and stderr go"
    echo "  to a scratch file, polled from later calls. Started as a background"
    echo "  task of the calling session."
    echo "TERMS: the four debug builds were finished by gate.log before this run"
    echo "  started, so no cargo runs during it; order host then i686; nothing"
    echo "  else running; no mid-run tuning, and a copy or conversion that timed"
    echo "  out or was killed would be recorded and listed apart, never rerun with"
    echo "  a larger value."
    echo "TIMEOUT CHOSEN BEFORE THE RUN: --timeout 300 for the copy child, the"
    echo "  figure part 4's runs used: M1 part 2 P1 and P2 measured the largest"
    echo "  corpus workbook, whose largest part is 63745347 bytes, at about 28"
    echo "  seconds with the host debug binary and about 30 with the i686 one."
    echo "  --style-sample reads the workbook part, the styles part and the"
    echo "  first worksheet, records two format additions and two cell edits,"
    echo "  writes the archive and reopens it to read the edit back. The figure"
    echo "  is not tuned during the run."
    echo "Workbooks are cited by id only. The corpus directory's PATH is written"
    echo "  <corpus> wherever this log prints a path; its NAME appears in the"
    echo "  script printed below, in the line that takes the default CLAUDE.md"
    echo "  gives. What is private is the corpus's contents and file names."
    echo
    echo "## script"
    echo "command: sed 's/^/    /' <this script>; sha256 $(sha256sum <"$0" | cut -d' ' -f1), $(wc -c <"$0") bytes"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$0"
    echo
    echo "## the comparison this log runs (python3, zipfile and expat)"
    cat >"$W/cmp.py" <<'CMP_PY'
    """The run log's own style comparison (specs/0012, "Harness runs", P2).
    
    Usage: cmp.py <input archive> <output archive> [--plant <flag>]
           cmp.py <input archive> --parts
    
    Reads the package's own relationships with zipfile and expat, sharing no code
    with the library or the tool, and makes its own pick of the edit
    --style-sample should have made: the first sheet of kind worksheet in
    <sheets> order, and in it A, the first cell in document order whose t is
    absent, "n" or "s", which has a <v> with text and no <f>, and M, the largest
    row number among its cells (0 for none). From the styles part it takes X (the
    <xf> children of <cellXfs>) and F (the <numFmt> children of <numFmts>).
    
    It then compares the two archives part by part.
    
    For the styles part, by bytes:
    
    - the bytes before <numFmts (or before <cellXfs when the input has no
      numFmts), the bytes from </numFmts> to <cellXfs, and the bytes from
      </cellXfs> to the end of the part are identical in input and output;
    - inside numFmts the input's children's bytes are a prefix of the output's,
      exactly one numFmt follows, its id is the largest input id plus one or 164
      when that is larger, and count grows by one;
    - inside cellXfs the input's children's bytes are a prefix of the output's,
      exactly two xf elements follow, the first carries numFmtId equal to that
      new id and applyNumberFormat="1", the second is byte for byte the string
      "Harness runs" gives for it (P2 ruling 2), and count grows by two.
    
    For the worksheet, as specs/0011's P2 comparison does: the bytes outside
    sheetData identical, and every cell as the tuple (reference, s, t, formula
    presence, value text, has <v>) counted unchanged, changed, added and removed.
    The changed references must be exactly A when A exists and none when it does
    not, with A's t, formula presence and value text the input's and its s alone
    different; the added reference must be exactly (M + 1, 1) with s equal to X +
    1; and nothing is removed.
    
    It prints ONE line of counts and yes/no flags: no reference, no value, no
    text, no format code and no part name. With --parts it prints two part names
    on two lines (the sheet and the styles part, or nothing) for the log to
    compare with the runner's entry rows; the log never prints them.
    
    --plant <flag> makes one planted difference in the output before the
    comparison, chosen so that the named flag, and in general that flag alone,
    turns from yes to no: the control for every flag this comparison raises.
    """
    import posixpath
    import re
    import sys
    import xml.parsers.expat
    import zipfile
    
    MAIN = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/spreadsheetml/main")
    RELS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships"
    ATTR = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/officeDocument/relationships")
    
    
    def rels_name(part):
        d, base = posixpath.split(part)
        return posixpath.join(d, "_rels", base + ".rels") if base else "_rels/.rels"
    
    
    def rels_of(z, part):
        d = posixpath.dirname(part)
        name = rels_name(part)
        out = []
        if name not in z.namelist():
            return out
        found = []
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            if tag == RELS + " Relationship" and attrs.get("TargetMode") != "External":
                found.append(attrs)
        p = xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate(namespace_separator=" ")
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.Parse(z.read(name), True)
        for a in found:
            target = a.get("Target", "")
            resolved = (target[1:] if target.startswith("/")
                        else posixpath.normpath(posixpath.join(d, target)))
            out.append((a.get("Id"), a.get("Type", ""), resolved))
        return out
    
    
    def workbook_of(z):
        office = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, "") if ty.endswith("/officeDocument")]
        return office[0] if len(office) == 1 else None
    
    
    def worksheets(z, workbook):
        by_id = {i: (ty, t) for (i, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook)}
        order = []
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            ns, _, local = tag.rpartition(" ")
            if ns in MAIN and local == "sheet":
                for a in ATTR:
                    if a + " id" in attrs:
                        order.append(attrs[a + " id"])
        p = xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate(namespace_separator=" ")
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.Parse(z.read(workbook), True)
        out = []
        for rid in order:
            ty, target = by_id.get(rid, ("", None))
            if ty.endswith("/worksheet") and target in z.namelist():
                out.append(target)
        return out
    
    
    def chain_of(z, workbook):
        chains = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook) if ty.endswith("/calcChain")]
        return chains[0] if chains else None
    
    
    def cells(data):
        """{reference: tuple}, the document order, the <row> count, and the
        first cell with a normal formula."""
        out = {}
        order = []
        stack = []
        state = {"cell": None, "text": None, "rows": 0, "normal": None}
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            ns, _, local = tag.rpartition(" ")
            local = local if ns in MAIN else None
            stack.append(local)
            if local == "row" and stack[-2:-1] == ["sheetData"]:
                state["rows"] += 1
            if local == "c" and stack[-2:-1] == ["row"] and stack[-3:-2] == ["sheetData"]:
                state["cell"] = {"r": attrs.get("r"), "s": attrs.get("s"),
                                 "t": attrs.get("t"), "f": False, "normal": False,
                                 "v": None, "is": None}
            elif state["cell"] is not None:
                if local == "f" and stack[-2:-1] == ["c"]:
                    state["cell"]["f"] = True
                    state["cell"]["normal"] = attrs.get("t", "normal") == "normal"
                elif local == "v" and stack[-2:-1] == ["c"]:
                    state["text"] = "v"
                    state["cell"]["v"] = ""
                elif local == "is" and stack[-2:-1] == ["c"]:
                    state["cell"]["is"] = ""
                elif local == "t" and "is" in stack:
                    state["text"] = "is"
    
        def end(tag):
            local = stack.pop()
            if local in ("v", "t"):
                state["text"] = None
            if local == "c" and state["cell"] is not None and stack[-1:] == ["row"]:
                c = state["cell"]
                value = c["v"] if c["v"] is not None else c["is"]
                out[c["r"]] = (c["r"], c["s"], c["t"], c["f"], value, c["v"] is not None)
                order.append(c["r"])
                if c["normal"] and state["normal"] is None:
                    state["normal"] = c["r"]
                state["cell"] = None
    
        def chars(text):
            if state["cell"] is not None and state["text"] is not None:
                state["cell"][state["text"]] += text
    
        p = xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate(namespace_separator=" ")
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.EndElementHandler = end
        p.CharacterDataHandler = chars
        p.buffer_text = True
        p.Parse(data, True)
        return out, order, state["rows"], state["normal"]
    
    
    def bounds(data):
        """(prefix end, end tag start or None for <sheetData/>, element end)."""
        start = re.search(rb"<([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?sheetData[\s/>]", data)
        if start is None:
            return None
        close = data.find(b">", start.start())
        if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
            return start.start(), None, close + 1
        ends = list(re.finditer(rb"</([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?sheetData\s*>", data))
        if not ends:
            return None
        return start.start(), ends[-1].start(), ends[-1].end()
    
    
    
    
    def styles_of(z, workbook):
        """The styles part the workbook names, or None."""
        parts = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook) if ty.endswith("/styles")]
        return parts[0] if parts and parts[0] in z.namelist() else None
    
    
    def container(data, name):
        """The spans of one root child: (start of its start tag, start of its
        children, end of its children, end of the element), or None when the part
        has no such element. An empty element has equal child bounds."""
        start = re.search(rb"<([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?" + name + rb"[\s/>]", data)
        if start is None:
            return None
        close = data.find(b">", start.start())
        if close < 0:
            return None
        if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
            return start.start(), close + 1, close + 1, close + 1
        ends = list(re.finditer(rb"</([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?" + name + rb"\s*>", data))
        if not ends:
            return None
        return start.start(), close + 1, ends[-1].start(), ends[-1].end()
    
    
    def count_attribute(data, span):
        """The count attribute of the start tag at span, as an int, or None."""
        tag = data[span[0]:span[1]]
        found = re.search(rb"\scount\s*=\s*(\"[^\"]*\"|'[^']*')", tag)
        if found is None:
            return None
        try:
            return int(found.group(1)[1:-1])
        except ValueError:
            return None
    
    
    def elements(data):
        """The (name, attributes, bytes) of every top-level element in data,
        which is a container's children."""
        out = []
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            ns, _, local = tag.rpartition(" ")
            out.append((local if ns in MAIN else None, attrs))
        p = xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate(namespace_separator=" ")
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.Parse(b"<r xmlns='" + MAIN[0].encode() + b"'>" + data + b"</r>", True)
        return out[1:]
    
    
    def num_fmt_ids(data):
        """The numFmtId of every numFmt among a numFmts container's children."""
        out = []
        for (local, attrs) in elements(data):
            if local == "numFmt" and "numFmtId" in attrs:
                try:
                    out.append(int(attrs["numFmtId"]))
                except ValueError:
                    pass
        return out
    
    
    def top_level(data):
        """The children's bytes cut into one span per top-level element, so an
        addition can be counted and read without a parser that keeps offsets."""
        spans = []
        depth = 0
        at = 0
        i = 0
        while i < len(data):
            if data[i:i + 1] == b"<" and data[i + 1:i + 2] not in (b"/", b"!", b"?"):
                if depth == 0:
                    at = i
                close = data.find(b">", i)
                if close < 0:
                    break
                empty = data[close - 1:close] == b"/"
                if empty:
                    if depth == 0:
                        spans.append((at, close + 1))
                else:
                    depth += 1
                i = close + 1
                continue
            if data[i:i + 2] == b"</":
                close = data.find(b">", i)
                if close < 0:
                    break
                depth -= 1
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((at, close + 1))
                i = close + 1
                continue
            i += 1
        return spans
    
    
    def col_of(reference):
        """The 1-based column of an A1 reference."""
        letters = re.match(r"[A-Za-z]+", reference or "")
        if letters is None:
            return 0
        n = 0
        for ch in letters.group(0).upper():
            n = n * 26 + (ord(ch) - 64)
        return n
    
    
    def row_of(reference):
        digits = re.search(r"\d+", reference or "")
        return int(digits.group(0)) if digits else 0
    
    
    def a1(row, col):
        name = ""
        while col > 0:
            col, rest = divmod(col - 1, 26)
            name = chr(65 + rest) + name
        return "%s%d" % (name, row)
    
    
    def sampled(data):
        """A (the first cell of a sampled kind with a value and no formula), M
        (the largest row among the cells) and the cell count of one sheet."""
        found, order, _, _ = cells(data)
        a = None
        top = 0
        for ref in order:
            (_, _, t, formula, value, has_v) = found[ref]
            top = max(top, row_of(ref))
            candidate = (t in (None, "n", "s") and has_v and value is not None
                         and value != "" and not formula)
            if candidate and a is None:
                a = ref
        return a, top, found, order
    
    
    def pick(z):
        """The workbook, its first worksheet, its styles part, A and M."""
        workbook = workbook_of(z)
        if workbook is None:
            return None, None, None, None, 0
        sheets = worksheets(z, workbook)
        part = sheets[0] if sheets else None
        styles = styles_of(z, workbook)
        if part is None:
            return workbook, None, styles, None, 0
        a, top, _, _ = sampled(z.read(part))
        return workbook, part, styles, a, top
    
    
    PLANTS = (
        "head_same", "mid_same", "tail_same", "fmts_prefix", "fmt_added",
        "fmt_id_ok", "fmt_count_grew", "xfs_prefix", "xfs_added", "coded_xf_ok",
        "dated_xf_ok", "xf_count_grew", "ws_prefix_same", "ws_suffix_same",
        "changed_as_styled", "added_as_edited", "nothing_removed",
        # Not a flag: a second plant for dated_xf_ok that keeps every attribute
        # and value and only reorders them, which byte equality must catch
        # (P2 ruling 2).
        "dated_xf_order",
    )
    
    
    def plant_styles(data, flag, ids, fmts_in):
        """The planted difference for a styles-part flag, and whether it applied.
    
        A plant that cannot falsify its flag on this pair does not apply, and
        says so rather than leaving a flag that passes for want of a difference:
        an input with no numFmts of its own makes the prefix flag vacuous, since
        every byte string starts with an empty one.
        """
        fmts = container(data, b"numFmts")
        xfs = container(data, b"cellXfs")
        if flag == "head_same":
            # Just before the first of the two containers, which is where the
            # head span ends: a comment there lands in the head and nowhere else.
            at = fmts[0] if fmts is not None else xfs[0]
            return data[:at] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[at:], True
        if flag == "mid_same" and fmts is not None:
            return data[:fmts[3]] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[fmts[3]:], True
        if flag == "tail_same":
            return data[:xfs[3]] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[xfs[3]:], True
        if flag == "fmts_prefix" and fmts is not None and fmts_in:
            spans = top_level(data[fmts[1]:fmts[2]])
            if spans:
                at = fmts[1] + spans[0][0]
                return data[:at] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[at:], True
        if flag == "fmt_added" and fmts is not None:
            return data[:fmts[2]] + b'<numFmt numFmtId="199" formatCode="0.0000"/>' + data[fmts[2]:], True
        if flag == "fmt_id_ok" and fmts is not None:
            spans = top_level(data[fmts[1]:fmts[2]])
            if spans:
                last = data[fmts[1] + spans[-1][0]:fmts[1] + spans[-1][1]]
                other = re.sub(rb'numFmtId\s*=\s*"\d+"', b'numFmtId="199"', last, count=1)
                return data[:fmts[1] + spans[-1][0]] + other + data[fmts[1] + spans[-1][1]:], True
        if flag == "fmt_count_grew" and fmts is not None:
            tag = data[fmts[0]:fmts[1]]
            # Zero is never the count a growing container should carry, whatever
            # the input held, so this plant is wrong on every pair.
            return data[:fmts[0]] + re.sub(rb'count\s*=\s*"\d+"', b'count="0"', tag, count=1) \
                + data[fmts[1]:], True
        if flag == "xfs_prefix":
            spans = top_level(data[xfs[1]:xfs[2]])
            if spans:
                at = xfs[1] + spans[0][0]
                return data[:at] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[at:], True
        if flag == "xfs_added":
            return data[:xfs[2]] + b"<xf/>" + data[xfs[2]:], True
        if flag in ("coded_xf_ok", "dated_xf_ok"):
            spans = top_level(data[xfs[1]:xfs[2]])
            which = -2 if flag == "coded_xf_ok" else -1
            if len(spans) >= 2:
                at = xfs[1] + spans[which][0]
                to = xfs[1] + spans[which][1]
                return data[:at] + b'<xf numFmtId="0"/>' + data[to:], True
        if flag == "dated_xf_order":
            spans = top_level(data[xfs[1]:xfs[2]])
            if len(spans) >= 2:
                at = xfs[1] + spans[-1][0]
                to = xfs[1] + spans[-1][1]
                return data[:at] + DATED_XF_REORDERED + data[to:], True
        if flag == "xf_count_grew":
            tag = data[xfs[0]:xfs[1]]
            return data[:xfs[0]] + re.sub(rb'count\s*=\s*"\d+"', b'count="0"', tag, count=1) \
                + data[xfs[1]:], True
        return data, False
    
    
    def cell_spans(data, upto):
        """One span per top-level <c> element inside sheetData."""
        spans = []
        for hit in re.finditer(rb"<([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?c[\s/>]", data[:upto]):
            at = hit.start()
            close = data.find(b">", at)
            if close < 0:
                break
            if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
                spans.append((at, close + 1))
                continue
            end = re.compile(rb"</([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?c\s*>").search(data, close)
            if end is None:
                break
            spans.append((at, end.end()))
        return spans
    
    
    def reference_of(span_bytes):
        hit = re.search(rb'\sr\s*=\s*"([^"]*)"', span_bytes)
        return hit.group(1).decode("ascii", "replace") if hit else ""
    
    
    def plant_sheet(data, flag, a, added):  # noqa: C901
        """The planted difference for a worksheet flag, or the bytes unchanged.
    
        A cell the edit itself touched is never the target: a plant on A or on
        the added cell would leave the flag it is meant to turn as it was.
        """
        span = bounds(data)
        if span is None:
            return data, False
        rows = list(re.finditer(rb"<([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?row[\s/>]", data))
        prefix = rows[-1].group(1) if rows and rows[-1].group(1) else b""
        at = span[1] if span[1] is not None else span[2]
        if flag == "ws_prefix_same":
            return data[:span[0]] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[span[0]:], True
        if flag == "ws_suffix_same":
            return data[:span[2]] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[span[2]:], True
        if flag == "added_as_edited":
            # Inside the last row, not beside it: a <c> that is not a row's child
            # is no cell, so a plant there would be read as no difference at all.
            cell = (b"<" + prefix + b'c r="ZZ999998" s="0"><' + prefix + b"v>0</"
                    + prefix + b"v></" + prefix + b"c>")
            close = data.rfind(b"</" + prefix + b"row>", 0, at)
            if close < 0:
                row = (b"<" + prefix + b'row r="999998">' + cell + b"</" + prefix + b"row>")
                return data[:at] + row + data[at:], True
            return data[:close] + cell + data[close:], True
        if flag in ("changed_as_styled", "nothing_removed"):
            spans = [s for s in cell_spans(data, at)
                     if reference_of(data[s[0]:s[1]]) not in (a, added)]
            if not spans:
                return data, False
            start, end = spans[-1]
            if flag == "nothing_removed":
                return data[:start] + data[end:], True
            # One more changed cell: its `s` is set to a value it did not carry,
            # which is exactly what the flag says only A may have.
            cell = data[start:end]
            if re.search(rb'\ss\s*=\s*"[^"]*"', cell):
                other = re.sub(rb'\ss\s*=\s*"[^"]*"', b' s="0"', cell, count=1)
                if other == cell:
                    other = re.sub(rb'\ss\s*=\s*"[^"]*"', b' s="1"', cell, count=1)
            else:
                close = cell.find(b">")
                cut = close - 1 if cell[close - 1:close] == b"/" else close
                other = cell[:cut] + b' s="0"' + cell[cut:]
            if other == cell:
                return data, False
            return data[:start] + other + data[end:], True
        return data, False
    
    
    # The second added xf, exactly as "Harness runs" P2 writes it (P2 ruling 2).
    DATED_XF = (b'<xf numFmtId="14" fontId="0" fillId="0" borderId="0" xfId="0" '
                b'applyNumberFormat="1"/>')
    # The same attributes and values in another order: the reorder plant.
    DATED_XF_REORDERED = (b'<xf fontId="0" numFmtId="14" fillId="0" borderId="0" xfId="0" '
                          b'applyNumberFormat="1"/>')
    
    
    def creation_point(data, fallback):
        """Where a numFmts the part does not have is created: the start of the
        first of fonts, fills, borders, cellStyleXfs and cellXfs that the part
        holds, whichever comes first in the part's own order."""
        starts = []
        for name in (b"fonts", b"fills", b"borders", b"cellStyleXfs", b"cellXfs"):
            span = container(data, name)
            if span is not None:
                starts.append(span[0])
        return min(starts) if starts else fallback
    
    
    def styles_flags(din, dout, expect_id):
        """Every styles-part flag, by bytes, and the two counts the line carries.
    
        A part with no numFmts of its own is the case the spec names: the head
        then runs to <cellXfs and the created container is the addition itself.
        """
        out = {}
        fin, fout = container(din, b"numFmts"), container(dout, b"numFmts")
        xin, xout = container(din, b"cellXfs"), container(dout, b"cellXfs")
        if xin is None or xout is None or fout is None:
            return None, 0, 0
        # Where a created numFmts goes: before the first of the five the part
        # holds, in the part's own order (specs/0012, P1 verification ruling 5).
        # For a part that has one already the head simply ends at it.
        cut = fin[0] if fin is not None else creation_point(din, xin[0])
        out["head_same"] = din[:cut] == dout[:fout[0]]
        out["mid_same"] = din[fin[3] if fin is not None else cut:xin[0]] \
            == dout[fout[3]:xout[0]]
        out["tail_same"] = din[xin[3]:] == dout[xout[3]:]
    
        fmts_in = din[fin[1]:fin[2]] if fin is not None else b""
        fmts_out = dout[fout[1]:fout[2]]
        out["fmts_prefix"] = fmts_out.startswith(fmts_in)
        rest = top_level(fmts_out[len(fmts_in):])
        added_fmts = [fmts_out[len(fmts_in):][s[0]:s[1]] for s in rest]
        out["fmt_added"] = len(added_fmts) == 1 and num_fmt_ids(added_fmts[0]) != []
        ids = num_fmt_ids(added_fmts[0]) if out["fmt_added"] else []
        out["fmt_id_ok"] = ids == [expect_id]
        count_in = count_attribute(din, fin) if fin is not None else 0
        count_out = count_attribute(dout, fout)
        fmts_before = len(num_fmt_ids(fmts_in))
        fmts_after = len(num_fmt_ids(fmts_out))
        # The library writes the container's count from its CHILDREN plus the
        # additions, not from whatever the input's attribute said, so that is
        # what this flag holds it to: the output's count is its own children's
        # number, and that number is one more than the input's. Whether the
        # input's own attribute agreed with its children is a property of the
        # INPUT and is reported beside the flag rather than folded into it.
        out["fmt_count_grew"] = count_out is not None and count_out == fmts_after \
            and fmts_after == fmts_before + 1
        out["_fmt_count_in_matched"] = (count_in or 0) == fmts_before
    
        xfs_in = din[xin[1]:xin[2]]
        xfs_out = dout[xout[1]:xout[2]]
        out["xfs_prefix"] = xfs_out.startswith(xfs_in)
        spans = top_level(xfs_out[len(xfs_in):])
        added_xfs = [xfs_out[len(xfs_in):][s[0]:s[1]] for s in spans]
        out["xfs_added"] = len(added_xfs) == 2
        coded = added_xfs[0] if out["xfs_added"] else b""
        dated = added_xfs[1] if out["xfs_added"] else b""
        out["coded_xf_ok"] = (b'numFmtId="%d"' % expect_id) in coded \
            and b'applyNumberFormat="1"' in coded
        out["dated_xf_ok"] = dated == DATED_XF
        xfs_count_in = count_attribute(din, xin)
        xfs_count_out = count_attribute(dout, xout)
        xfs_in_n = len(top_level(xfs_in))
        xfs_out_n = len(top_level(xfs_out))
        out["xf_count_grew"] = xfs_count_out is not None and xfs_count_out == xfs_out_n \
            and xfs_out_n == xfs_in_n + 2
        out["_xf_count_in_matched"] = xfs_count_in == xfs_in_n
        return out, xfs_in_n, fmts_after - fmts_before
    
    
    def main():
        zin = zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[1])
        workbook, part, styles, a, top = pick(zin)
        if sys.argv[2:3] == ["--parts"]:
            print(part or "")
            print(styles or "")
            return
        zout = zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[2])
        plant = None
        if "--plant" in sys.argv[3:]:
            plant = sys.argv[sys.argv.index("--plant") + 1]
            if plant not in PLANTS:
                print("error=unknown-plant")
                return
        yn = lambda v: "yes" if v else "no"
        if part is None or styles is None:
            print("found=0")
            return
        added = a1(top + 1, 1)
        sin, sout = zin.read(styles), zout.read(styles)
        din, dout = zin.read(part), zout.read(part)
        ids = num_fmt_ids(sin[container(sin, b"numFmts")[1]:container(sin, b"numFmts")[2]]) \
            if container(sin, b"numFmts") is not None else []
        expect_id = max(164, max(ids) + 1) if ids else 164
        planted = True
        if plant is not None:
            fmts_in = container(sin, b"numFmts") is not None
            sout, in_styles = plant_styles(sout, plant, ids, fmts_in)
            dout, in_sheet = plant_sheet(dout, plant, a, added)
            planted = in_styles or in_sheet
    
        flags, xfs_before, formats_added = styles_flags(sin, sout, expect_id)
        if flags is None:
            print("error=no-container")
            return
        out_xfs = container(sout, b"cellXfs")
        xfs_after = len(top_level(sout[out_xfs[1]:out_xfs[2]]))
    
        bi, bo = bounds(din), bounds(dout)
        if bi is None or bo is None:
            print("error=no-sheetData")
            return
        ws_prefix_same = din[:bi[0]] == dout[:bo[0]]
        if bi[1] is not None and bo[1] is not None:
            ws_suffix_same = din[bi[1]:] == dout[bo[1]:]
        else:
            ws_suffix_same = din[bi[2]:] == dout[bo[2]:]
        cin, _, _, _ = cells(din)
        cout, _, _, _ = cells(dout)
        unchanged = changed = removed = 0
        changed_refs = set()
        for ref, tup in cin.items():
            if ref not in cout:
                removed += 1
            elif cout[ref] == tup:
                unchanged += 1
            else:
                changed += 1
                changed_refs.add(ref)
        added_refs = set(cout) - set(cin)
        styled = 1 if a is not None else 0
        if a is not None and a in cout and a in cin:
            # A's `s` alone differs: its t, formula presence and value are the
            # input's, and its new `s` is the first of the two added formats.
            a_kept = cout[a][2:] == cin[a][2:] and cout[a][1] != cin[a][1] \
                and cout[a][1] == str(xfs_before)
        else:
            a_kept = a is None
        changed_as_styled = changed == styled and changed_refs == ({a} if a else set()) \
            and a_kept
        added_as_edited = added_refs == {added} and added in cout \
            and cout[added][1] == str(xfs_before + 1) \
            and col_of(added) == 1 and row_of(added) == top + 1
        print(" ".join([
            "found=1", "planted=%s" % yn(planted), "styled=%d" % styled,
            "xfs_before=%d" % xfs_before,
            "xfs_after=%d" % xfs_after,
            "formats_added=%d" % formats_added,
            "cells_in=%d" % len(cin), "cells_out=%d" % len(cout),
            "unchanged=%d" % unchanged, "changed=%d" % changed,
            "added=%d" % len(added_refs), "removed=%d" % removed,
        ] + ["%s=%s" % (name, yn(flags[name])) for name in (
            "head_same", "mid_same", "tail_same", "fmts_prefix", "fmt_added",
            "fmt_id_ok", "fmt_count_grew", "xfs_prefix", "xfs_added",
            "coded_xf_ok", "dated_xf_ok", "xf_count_grew")]
          + ["fmt_count_in_matched=%s" % yn(flags["_fmt_count_in_matched"]),
             "xf_count_in_matched=%s" % yn(flags["_xf_count_in_matched"]),
             "ws_prefix_same=%s" % yn(ws_prefix_same),
             "ws_suffix_same=%s" % yn(ws_suffix_same),
             "changed_as_styled=%s" % yn(changed_as_styled),
             "added_as_edited=%s" % yn(added_as_edited),
             "nothing_removed=%s" % yn(removed == 0)]))
    
    
    main()
    CMP_PY
    sed "s/^/    /" "$W/cmp.py"
    
    echo
    echo "## the comparison's own controls, on generated pairs"
    echo "The three inputs below are written here, byte for byte as the script"
    echo "  says, and edited by the host debug binary this run uses. Their"
    echo "  contents are fictional. The corpus is not touched by this section."
    cat >"$W/make.py" <<'MAKE_PY'
    """Three fictional packages for the comparison's controls.
    
    Usage: make.py <directory>
    
      sample.xlsx   a sheet with a styled number, a shared string and a formula,
                    and a styles part with one numFmt and three xfs;
      empty.xlsx    the same styles part and a sheet with no cells at all, so the
                    sample has no A and styles the new cell alone;
      nofmts.xlsx   a styles part with NO numFmts of its own, so the edit creates
                    the container (P1 verification ruling 5).
    """
    import os
    import sys
    import zipfile
    
    MAIN = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main"
    RELS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships"
    ATTR = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships"
    TYPES = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/content-types"
    DECL = '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>'
    
    WITH_FMTS = ('<styleSheet xmlns="%s"><numFmts count="1">'
                 '<numFmt numFmtId="164" formatCode="0.00"/></numFmts>'
                 '<fonts count="1"><font><name val="Fictional"/></font></fonts>'
                 '<cellXfs count="3"><xf numFmtId="0"/>'
                 '<xf numFmtId="164" fontId="0"/><xf/></cellXfs></styleSheet>' % MAIN)
    NO_FMTS = ('<styleSheet xmlns="%s">'
               '<fonts count="1"><font><name val="Fictional"/></font></fonts>'
               '<cellXfs count="2"><xf numFmtId="0"/>'
               '<xf numFmtId="9" fontId="0"/></cellXfs></styleSheet>' % MAIN)
    CELLS = ('<sheetData><row r="1"><c r="A1" s="1"><v>1.5</v></c>'
             '<c r="B1" t="s"><v>1</v></c></row>'
             '<row r="2"><c r="A2"><f>A1*2</f><v>3</v></c>'
             '<c r="C2" s="2"><v>7</v></c></row></sheetData>')
    
    
    def build(path, sheet_data, styles):
        parts = {
            "[Content_Types].xml": DECL + (
                '<Types xmlns="%s"><Default Extension="rels" ContentType="application/rels"/>'
                '<Default Extension="xml" ContentType="application/xml"/>'
                '<Override PartName="/xl/workbook.xml" ContentType="application/workbook"/>'
                '<Override PartName="/xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml" ContentType="application/sheet"/>'
                '<Override PartName="/xl/styles.xml" ContentType="application/styles"/>'
                "</Types>" % TYPES),
            "_rels/.rels": (
                '<Relationships xmlns="%s"><Relationship Id="rId1" Type="%s/officeDocument" '
                'Target="xl/workbook.xml"/></Relationships>' % (RELS, ATTR)),
            "xl/workbook.xml": DECL + (
                '<workbook xmlns="%s" xmlns:r="%s"><sheets>'
                '<sheet name="Sheet1" sheetId="1" r:id="rId1"/></sheets></workbook>' % (MAIN, ATTR)),
            "xl/_rels/workbook.xml.rels": (
                '<Relationships xmlns="%s">'
                '<Relationship Id="rId1" Type="%s/worksheet" Target="worksheets/sheet1.xml"/>'
                '<Relationship Id="rId2" Type="%s/styles" Target="styles.xml"/>'
                "</Relationships>" % (RELS, ATTR, ATTR)),
            "xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml": DECL + (
                '<worksheet xmlns="%s"><dimension ref="A1"/>%s'
                '<pageMargins left="0.7"/></worksheet>' % (MAIN, sheet_data)),
            "xl/styles.xml": DECL + styles,
        }
        with zipfile.ZipFile(path, "w", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:
            for name, text in parts.items():
                z.writestr(name, text)
    
    
    d = sys.argv[1]
    build(os.path.join(d, "sample.xlsx"), CELLS, WITH_FMTS)
    build(os.path.join(d, "empty.xlsx"), "<sheetData/>", WITH_FMTS)
    build(os.path.join(d, "nofmts.xlsx"),
          '<sheetData><row r="1"><c r="A1" s="1"><v>2.5</v></c></row></sheetData>', NO_FMTS)
    MAKE_PY
    echo "the generator this section runs:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/make.py"
    mkdir -p "$W/ctl"
    python3 "$W/make.py" "$W/ctl"
    echo "command: python3 make.py <scratch>/ctl; then target/debug/emend-copy <in> <out> --style-sample"
    
    # The seventeen flags the comparison raises, in the order it prints them.
    FLAGS='head_same mid_same tail_same fmts_prefix fmt_added fmt_id_ok fmt_count_grew
           xfs_prefix xfs_added coded_xf_ok dated_xf_ok xf_count_grew ws_prefix_same
           ws_suffix_same changed_as_styled added_as_edited nothing_removed'
    # flag_value <line> <flag>: the yes or no the comparison printed for one flag.
    flag_value() { kv "$1" "$2"; }
    # all_yes <line>: every flag in the line reads yes.
    all_yes() {
      for f in $FLAGS; do
        [ "$(flag_value "$1" "$f")" = yes ] || return 1
      done
      return 0
    }
    # plant_bit <line> <flag>: the plant turned its own flag to no.
    plant_bit() { [ "$(flag_value "$1" "$2")" = no ]; }
    # plant_absent <line> <flag>: the plant did not apply, and says so, and the
    # flag it could not falsify is still yes.
    plant_absent() {
      [ "$(kv "$1" planted)" = no ] && [ "$(flag_value "$1" "$2")" = yes ]
    }
    # only_dated_no <line>: dated_xf_ok reads no and every other flag yes, the
    # reading the reorder plant must produce (P2 ruling 2).
    only_dated_no() {
      [ "$(flag_value "$1" dated_xf_ok)" = no ] || return 1
      for f in $FLAGS; do
        [ "$f" = dated_xf_ok ] && continue
        [ "$(flag_value "$1" "$f")" = yes ] || return 1
      done
      return 0
    }
    # plant_accounted <line> <flag>: either of the two above, and nothing else.
    plant_accounted() {
      if plant_bit "$1" "$2"; then return 0; fi
      plant_absent "$1" "$2"
    }
    
    # tool_and_cmp <tool line> <comparison line>: the two lines agree on every
    # key they share. The tool counts through the library; the comparison counts
    # through zipfile and expat; neither sees the other's work.
    tool_and_cmp() {
      [ "$(kvn "$1" styled)" = "$(kvn "$2" styled)" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kvn "$1" xfs_before)" = "$(kvn "$2" xfs_before)" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kvn "$1" xfs_after)" = "$(kvn "$2" xfs_after)" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kvn "$1" formats_added)" = "$(kvn "$2" formats_added)" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kvn "$1" cells_before)" = "$(kvn "$2" cells_in)" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kvn "$1" cells_after)" = "$(kvn "$2" cells_out)" ]
    }
    # read_back_as_spec <tool line> <comparison line>: read_back is styled plus
    # two, the figure "Harness runs" states for every file.
    read_back_as_spec() {
      [ "$(kvn "$1" read_back)" = "$(( $(kvn "$2" styled) + 2 ))" ]
    }
    
    nctl=0
    for name in sample empty nofmts; do
      in_file=$W/ctl/$name.xlsx
      out_file=$W/ctl/$name-out.xlsx
      rm -f "$out_file"
      target/debug/emend-copy "$in_file" "$out_file" --style-sample >"$W/ctl/$name.line" 2>"$W/ctl/$name.err"
      crc=$?
      line=$(cat "$W/ctl/$name.line")
      cmpline=$(python3 "$W/cmp.py" "$in_file" "$out_file")
      echo "  $name: exit $crc; tool $(printf '%s' "$line" | tr '\t' ' ')"
      echo "  $name: cmp  $cmpline"
      if [ -s "$W/ctl/$name.err" ]; then hide <"$W/ctl/$name.err" | sed "s/^/    $name stderr: /"; fi
      note "control pair $name: the tool exits 0" "$(is [ "$crc" -eq 0 ])"
      note "control pair $name: every flag of the comparison reads yes" "$(is all_yes "$cmpline")"
      note "control pair $name: the tool's line and the comparison agree on every shared key" \
        "$(is tool_and_cmp "$line" "$cmpline")"
      note "control pair $name: read_back is styled plus two" \
        "$(is read_back_as_spec "$line" "$cmpline")"
      nbit=0; nabsent=0
      for f in $FLAGS; do
        planted=$(python3 "$W/cmp.py" "$in_file" "$out_file" --plant "$f")
        if plant_bit "$planted" "$f"; then
          nbit=$((nbit + 1))
        elif plant_absent "$planted" "$f"; then
          nabsent=$((nabsent + 1))
          echo "    $name: the plant for $f does not apply to this pair, and says so"
        fi
        note "control pair $name: the plant for $f is accounted for" \
          "$(is plant_accounted "$planted" "$f")"
      done
      reordered=$(python3 "$W/cmp.py" "$in_file" "$out_file" --plant dated_xf_order)
      echo "  $name: cmp with the reorder plant  $reordered"
      note "control pair $name: the reorder plant (same attributes, another order) turns dated_xf_ok to no and nothing else" \
        "$(is only_dated_no "$reordered")"
      echo "  $name: plants that turned their flag: $nbit; plants that do not apply: $nabsent"
      nctl=$((nctl + nbit))
    done
    echo "  planted faults that turned their own flag, over the three pairs: $nctl"
    all_flags_planted() { [ "$nctl" -ge 17 ]; }
    note "every flag the comparison raises was falsified by a plant on some pair" \
      "$(is all_flags_planted)"
    note "control: only_dated_no refuses a line where every flag reads yes" \
      "$(isnot only_dated_no "$(for f in $FLAGS; do printf '%s=yes ' "$f"; done)")"
    note "control: a line with no flags at all is refused by all_yes" \
      "$(isnot all_yes "found=1 planted=yes")"
    echo "## the column guard's own controls"
    printf 'id\tname\tstatus\tflags\n' >"$W/head.tsv"
    : >"$W/empty.tsv"
    printf 'id\tname\n' >"$W/short.tsv"
    COLUMNS_USED='id name status flags'
    note "columns_resolve accepts a header holding every column it indexes" \
      "$(is columns_resolve "$W/head.tsv" "$COLUMNS_USED")"
    note "columns_resolve refuses a header missing some of them" \
      "$(isnot columns_resolve "$W/short.tsv" "$COLUMNS_USED")"
    note "columns_resolve refuses an empty file" "$(isnot columns_resolve "$W/empty.tsv" "$COLUMNS_USED")"
    
    # entries_p2 <entries file> <id> <sheet part> <styles part>: the runner's
    # entry rows for one workbook are what P2 expects. Exactly two rows are
    # `changed`, and they are the two parts the comparison picked; every other
    # row is `identical` with no flag; a changed row may carry `descriptor` and
    # nothing else, as specs/0008 allows for a replaced entry. Names are read
    # here and never printed.
    entries_p2() {
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" -v sheet="$3" -v styles="$4" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next }
        $k["id"] != id { next }
        {
          n++
          name = $k["name"]; status = $k["status"]; flags = $k["flags"]
          if (status == "changed") {
            changed++
            if (name != sheet && name != styles) bad++
            if (flags != "" && flags != "descriptor") bad++
          } else if (status != "identical" || flags != "") {
            bad++
          }
        }
        END { exit (n == 0 || changed != 2 || bad > 0) }' "$1"
    }
    printf 'id\tname\tstatus\tflags\n' >"$W/e-ctl.tsv"
    printf 'w\ta.xml\tidentical\t\nw\tsheet1.xml\tchanged\t\nw\tstyles.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\n' \
      >>"$W/e-ctl.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 accepts the two changed parts, descriptor allowed" \
      "$(is entries_p2 "$W/e-ctl.tsv" w sheet1.xml styles.xml)"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses the same rows when another part is named" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-ctl.tsv" w sheet1.xml other.xml)"
    sed 's/a.xml\tidentical\t$/a.xml\tidentical\tdescriptor/' "$W/e-ctl.tsv" >"$W/e-flag.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses an identical row that carries a flag" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-flag.tsv" w sheet1.xml styles.xml)"
    sed 's/a.xml\tidentical\t$/a.xml\tchanged\t/' "$W/e-ctl.tsv" >"$W/e-three.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses a third changed row" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-three.tsv" w sheet1.xml styles.xml)"
    sed 's/styles.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor$/styles.xml\tchanged\trecompressed/' "$W/e-ctl.tsv" \
      >"$W/e-other.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses a changed row flagged anything but descriptor" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-other.tsv" w sheet1.xml styles.xml)"
    sed '/changed/d' "$W/e-ctl.tsv" >"$W/e-none.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses a workbook with no changed row" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-none.tsv" w sheet1.xml styles.xml)"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses an id with no rows" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-ctl.tsv" nosuchid sheet1.xml styles.xml)"
    
    echo
    echo "## settings"
    echo "  --timeout 300 (the copy child only); --lo-timeout 600 (per conversion,"
    echo "  input and copy each); image $LO_IMAGE; --tool-arg $EDIT"
    echo "  out directory: <corpus>/runs/$RUN"
    echo "  record stem: $STEM"
    # The debug binaries gate.log built and hashed (header change 1), each
    # compared with the hash that log printed, read out of it by command.
    GATE_LOG=records/logs/m1p5-p2/gate.log
    echo "command: read the four debug hashes from $GATE_LOG (sha256 $(sha256sum <"$GATE_LOG" | cut -d' ' -f1))"
    gate_hash() { sed -n "s#^  $1: sha256 \([0-9a-f]\{64\}\), bytes [0-9]*\$#\1#p" "$GATE_LOG"; }
    for b in target/debug/emend-copy target/debug/xlsx-diff \
             target/i686-unknown-linux-musl/debug/emend-copy \
             target/i686-unknown-linux-musl/debug/xlsx-diff; do
      if [ -x "$b" ]; then
        now=$(sha256sum <"$b" | cut -d' ' -f1)
        gated=$(gate_hash "$b")
        echo "  $b: sha256 $now; gate.log printed ${gated:-nothing}"
        note "$b is the binary gate.log hashed" "$(is [ "$now" = "$gated" ])"
      else
        echo "  $b: MISSING"; fail=1
      fi
    done
    note "control: the same reader finds no hash for a binary gate.log does not name" \
      "$(is [ -z "$(gate_hash target/debug/no-such-binary)" ])"
    echo "  (nothing is rebuilt here)"
    manifest_rows=$(nrows "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv")
    echo "  corpus manifest rows: $manifest_rows"
    note "the corpus holds its 27 workbooks" "$(is [ "$manifest_rows" = 27 ])"
    
    for label in host i686; do
      if [ "$label" = host ]; then
        PT=target/debug/emend-copy
        XD=target/debug/xlsx-diff
      else
        PT=target/i686-unknown-linux-musl/debug/emend-copy
        XD=target/i686-unknown-linux-musl/debug/xlsx-diff
      fi
      echo
      echo "## $label run, --tool-arg $EDIT"
      echo "command: scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label $label --passthrough $PT --xlsx-diff $XD --out <corpus>/runs/$RUN --libreoffice $LO_IMAGE --lo-timeout 600 --timeout 300 --tool-arg $EDIT"
      started=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label "$label" --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" \
        --out "$OUT" --libreoffice "$LO_IMAGE" --lo-timeout 600 --timeout 300 \
        --tool-arg "$EDIT" \
        >"$W/run-$label.stdout" 2>"$W/run-$label.stderr"
      rc=$?
      ended=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      echo "  started $started; ended $ended; exit $rc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$W/run-$label.stderr")"
      hide <"$W/run-$label.stdout" | sed 's/^/    /'
      if [ -s "$W/run-$label.stderr" ]; then hide <"$W/run-$label.stderr" | sed 's/^/    stderr: /'; fi
      note "$label the run exits 0" "$(is [ "$rc" -eq 0 ])"
      note "$label the run's stderr is empty" "$(is [ "$(wc -c <"$W/run-$label.stderr")" -eq 0 ])"
    
      SUM=$OUT/summary.$label.tsv
      ENT=$OUT/entries.$label.tsv
      if [ ! -f "$SUM" ] || [ ! -f "$ENT" ]; then
        echo "  the run wrote no summary or entries file"; fail=1; continue
      fi
      rows=$(nrows "$SUM")
      ok=$(count_where "$SUM" outcome ok)
      lo=$(count_where "$SUM" lo ok)
      lo_in=$(count_where "$SUM" lo_in ok)
      noleft=$(count_where "$SUM" leftover no)
      order=$(count_where "$SUM" order_preserved yes)
      comment=$(count_where "$SUM" comment_equal yes)
      fid_yes=$(count_where "$SUM" files_identical yes)
      echo "  summary rows: $rows; outcome ok: $ok; lo ok: $lo; lo_in ok: $lo_in; leftover no: $noleft"
      echo "  order_preserved yes: $order; comment_equal yes: $comment; files_identical yes: $fid_yes"
      echo "  entry totals from the summary: identical $(sum_col "$SUM" identical), recompressed $(sum_col "$SUM" recompressed), changed $(sum_col "$SUM" changed), dropped $(sum_col "$SUM" dropped), added $(sum_col "$SUM" added), flagged $(sum_col "$SUM" flagged)"
      note "$label every manifest workbook produced a summary row" "$(is [ "$rows" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
      note "$label every outcome is ok" "$(is [ "$ok" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label lo is ok on every file" "$(is [ "$lo" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label lo_in is ok on every file" "$(is [ "$lo_in" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label no tool left a temporary behind" "$(is [ "$noleft" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label order is preserved in every file" "$(is [ "$order" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label the archive comment is unchanged in every file" "$(is [ "$comment" = "$rows" ])"
      fid_no=$(count_where "$SUM" files_identical no)
      echo "  files_identical no: $fid_no"
      note "$label files_identical is no in all 27, since the edit writes" "$(is [ "$fid_no" = 27 ])"
      entries_as_p2() {
        # Two entries change in every workbook, the styles part and the first
        # worksheet, and nothing is recompressed, dropped or added.
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" changed)" = 54 ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" recompressed)$(sum_col "$SUM" dropped)$(sum_col "$SUM" added)" = 000 ]
      }
      note "$label 54 entries changed over the 27 workbooks and none moved otherwise" \
        "$(is entries_as_p2)"
    
      echo "  the entries header, as the runner wrote it:"
      echo "    $(head -1 "$ENT")"
      note "$label every column the entry form indexes is in that header" \
        "$(is columns_resolve "$ENT" "$COLUMNS_USED")"
    
      echo "  per workbook: id, the tool's edit line, the comparison's line"
      echo "  (counts and yes/no flags only; no reference, value, text, code or part name)"
      : >"$W/edits-$label"
      nwb=0; nagree=0; nentries_ok=0; nflags_ok=0; nread_ok=0
      t_xfs_after=0; t_formats=0; t_styled=0
      while IFS=$'\t' read -r id ext; do
        nwb=$((nwb + 1))
        in_file=$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext
        out_file=$OUT/$id/out.$label.$ext
        e=$(cat "$OUT/$id/stdout.$label.txt" 2>/dev/null)
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$e" >>"$W/edits-$label"
        c=$(python3 "$W/cmp.py" "$in_file" "$out_file")
        printf '    %s %s\n' "$id" "$(printf '%s' "$e" | tr '\t' ' ')"
        printf '    %s cmp %s\n' "$id" "$c"
        # The two parts the comparison picked, read into variables and never
        # printed: the entry rows are checked against them by name.
        python3 "$W/cmp.py" "$in_file" --parts >"$W/parts-$id"
        sheet_part=$(sed -n 1p "$W/parts-$id")
        styles_part=$(sed -n 2p "$W/parts-$id")
        if tool_and_cmp "$e" "$c"; then nagree=$((nagree + 1)); else echo "    $id: THE TOOL AND THE COMPARISON DISAGREE"; fi
        if all_yes "$c"; then nflags_ok=$((nflags_ok + 1)); else echo "    $id: a flag of the comparison does not hold"; fi
        if read_back_as_spec "$e" "$c"; then nread_ok=$((nread_ok + 1)); else echo "    $id: read_back is not styled plus two"; fi
        if entries_p2 "$ENT" "$id" "$sheet_part" "$styles_part"; then
          nentries_ok=$((nentries_ok + 1))
        else
          echo "    $id: the entry rows are not the two changed parts and the rest identical"
        fi
        t_xfs_after=$((t_xfs_after + $(kvn "$e" xfs_after)))
        t_formats=$((t_formats + $(kvn "$e" formats_added)))
        t_styled=$((t_styled + $(kvn "$e" styled)))
      done < <(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } { print $k["id"] "\t" $k["ext"] }' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv")
      echo "  workbooks: $nwb; the tool and the comparison agree: $nagree; every flag holds: $nflags_ok"
      echo "  read_back is styled plus two: $nread_ok; entry rows as P2 expects: $nentries_ok"
      echo "  $label totals from the tool's lines: xfs_after $t_xfs_after; formats_added $t_formats; styled $t_styled"
      note "$label the tool and the comparison agree on every shared key in all 27" "$(is [ "$nagree" = 27 ])"
      note "$label every flag of the comparison holds in all 27" "$(is [ "$nflags_ok" = 27 ])"
      note "$label read_back is styled plus two in all 27" "$(is [ "$nread_ok" = 27 ])"
      note "$label every workbook's entry rows are the two changed parts and the rest identical" \
        "$(is [ "$nentries_ok" = 27 ])"
      note "$label xfs_after totals 1046" "$(is [ "$t_xfs_after" = 1046 ])"
      note "$label formats_added totals 27" "$(is [ "$t_formats" = 27 ])"
    
      # The planted difference on a REAL pair: the first workbook's own output,
      # compared again with one flag's plant, must report that flag.
      first=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { print $1; exit }' "$W/edits-$label")
      first_ext=$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$first" 'NR > 1 && $1 == id { print $4 }' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv")
      e1=$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$first" '$1 == id { sub(/^[^\t]*\t/, ""); print }' "$W/edits-$label")
      c1=$(python3 "$W/cmp.py" "$CORPUS/corpus/$first.$first_ext" "$OUT/$first/out.$label.$first_ext")
      c1_plant=$(python3 "$W/cmp.py" "$CORPUS/corpus/$first.$first_ext" \
        "$OUT/$first/out.$label.$first_ext" --plant xfs_added)
      note "$label control: the first workbook's comparison holds as run" "$(is all_yes "$c1")"
      note "$label control: the same pair with an xf planted does not" "$(isnot all_yes "$c1_plant")"
      c1_order=$(python3 "$W/cmp.py" "$CORPUS/corpus/$first.$first_ext" \
        "$OUT/$first/out.$label.$first_ext" --plant dated_xf_order)
      note "$label control: the same pair with the dated xf's attributes reordered fails dated_xf_ok alone" \
        "$(is only_dated_no "$c1_order")"
      e1_plant=$(printf '%s' "$e1" | sed "s/\txfs_after=$(kvn "$e1" xfs_after)\t/\txfs_after=$(( $(kvn "$e1" xfs_after) + 1 ))\t/")
      note "$label control: the first workbook's line agrees with the comparison as run" \
        "$(is tool_and_cmp "$e1" "$c1")"
      note "$label control: the same line with xfs_after raised by one does not" \
        "$(isnot tool_and_cmp "$e1_plant" "$c1")"
    done
    echo
    echo "## the two labels agree"
    for label in host i686; do
      awk -F'\t' '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) idx[$i] = i; next }
        { print $idx["id"] "\t" $idx["name"] "\t" $idx["status"] "\t" $idx["flags"] }' \
        "$OUT/entries.$label.tsv" | sort >"$W/classes-$label"
      sort "$W/edits-$label" >"$W/edits-sorted-$label"
    done
    note "both targets classified every entry the same way" "$(is cmp -s "$W/classes-host" "$W/classes-i686")"
    note "both targets printed the same edit line for every workbook" \
      "$(is cmp -s "$W/edits-sorted-host" "$W/edits-sorted-i686")"
    note "control: the same comparison finds the host's lines differ from the i686 classes" \
      "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/edits-sorted-host" "$W/classes-i686")"
    
    echo
    echo "## the run rows both labels appended"
    for label in host i686; do
      R=$OUT/run.$label.tsv
      if [ -f "$R" ]; then
        echo "  run.$label.tsv header: $(head -1 "$R")"
        echo "  run.$label.tsv row: $(sed -n 2p "$R" | hide)"
        args=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "tool_args") k = i; next }
                           k && NR == 2 { print $k }' "$R")
        echo "  run.$label.tsv tool_args: [$args]"
        note "$label the run row records the operation" "$(is [ "$args" = "$EDIT" ])"
      else
        echo "  run.$label.tsv: MISSING"; fail=1
      fi
    done
    
    echo
    echo "## the record pair"
    echo "command: scripts/passthrough-record.py --run <corpus>/runs/$RUN --stem $STEM"
    scripts/passthrough-record.py --run "$OUT" --stem "$STEM" >"$W/record.out" 2>&1
    rrc=$?
    hide <"$W/record.out" | sed 's/^/    /'
    note "the record script exits 0" "$(is [ "$rrc" -eq 0 ])"
    for ext in md txt; do
      f=records/$STEM.$ext
      if [ -f "$f" ]; then
        echo "  $f: $(wc -c <"$f") bytes, sha256 $(sha256sum <"$f" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
      else
        echo "  $f: MISSING"; fail=1
      fi
    done
    both_halves() {
      [ -f "records/$STEM.md" ] || return 1
      [ -f "records/$STEM.txt" ] || return 1
    }
    note "both halves of the record pair were written" "$(is both_halves)"
    nargs=$(count_matches -F "$EDIT" "records/$STEM.md")
    echo "  lines of the record naming the operation: $nargs"
    note "the record names the operation it was run with" "$(is [ "$nargs" -ge 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the record pair holds no corpus path and no absolute path"
    for ext in md txt; do
      f=records/$STEM.$ext
      [ -f "$f" ] || continue
      n=$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|emend-testing)' "$f")
      echo "  $f: lines naming a home, mount or corpus path: $n"
      note "$f carries no such path" "$(is [ "$n" = 0 ])"
    done
    # The planted path is assembled at run time (P2 verification ruling 4), so
    # this script's own text carries no home-shaped path.
    printf '%s%s%s\n' '/ho' 'me/someone/' 'emend-testing/corpus/x.xlsx' >"$W/path-control"
    nctl=$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|emend-testing)' "$W/path-control")
    note "control: the path form finds a planted path ($nctl)" "$(is [ "$nctl" = 1 ])"
    
    
    echo
    echo "## status after the runs"
    # specs/0012-styles.md carries planning's "Planning rulings during P2"
    # uncommitted, as its ruling 8 says, at the hash planning gave; that one
    # modified file is accounted for by its hash and nothing else is.
    SPEC=specs/0012-styles.md
    SPEC_SHA=397da302b6f4911c758c2426463dcc1b10ac84c805aa67729bd3698574ef4b27
    spec_now=$(sha256sum <"$SPEC" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "  $SPEC: sha256 $spec_now; the hash planning's P2 rulings give: $SPEC_SHA"
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_log=$(run_matches -E '^(\?\?| ?[MARCD]) (records/logs/m1p5-p2|records/'"$STEM"')' git status --porcelain)
    st_spec=$(run_matches -E '^ M specs/0012-styles\.md$' git status --porcelain)
    echo "status lines: $st_all; of them under the phase log directory or the record pair: $st_log; the spec modified: $st_spec"
    spec_is_rulings() { [ "$st_spec" = 1 ] && [ "$spec_now" = "$SPEC_SHA" ]; }
    note "the one modified planning file is specs/0012 at the P2 rulings' hash" "$(is spec_is_rulings)"
    status_accounted() {
      [ "$st_all" != error ] && [ "$st_log" != error ] && [ "$st_spec" != error ] \
        && [ "$st_all" = "$((st_log + st_spec))" ]
    }
    note "every change in the working tree is a log, the record pair or that spec" "$(is status_accounted)"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "verdict rows other than as-expected: $nbad; of them marked UNEXPECTED: $nunexp"
    echo "run log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exit "$fail"

## the comparison this log runs (python3, zipfile and expat)
    """The run log's own style comparison (specs/0012, "Harness runs", P2).
    
    Usage: cmp.py <input archive> <output archive> [--plant <flag>]
           cmp.py <input archive> --parts
    
    Reads the package's own relationships with zipfile and expat, sharing no code
    with the library or the tool, and makes its own pick of the edit
    --style-sample should have made: the first sheet of kind worksheet in
    <sheets> order, and in it A, the first cell in document order whose t is
    absent, "n" or "s", which has a <v> with text and no <f>, and M, the largest
    row number among its cells (0 for none). From the styles part it takes X (the
    <xf> children of <cellXfs>) and F (the <numFmt> children of <numFmts>).
    
    It then compares the two archives part by part.
    
    For the styles part, by bytes:
    
    - the bytes before <numFmts (or before <cellXfs when the input has no
      numFmts), the bytes from </numFmts> to <cellXfs, and the bytes from
      </cellXfs> to the end of the part are identical in input and output;
    - inside numFmts the input's children's bytes are a prefix of the output's,
      exactly one numFmt follows, its id is the largest input id plus one or 164
      when that is larger, and count grows by one;
    - inside cellXfs the input's children's bytes are a prefix of the output's,
      exactly two xf elements follow, the first carries numFmtId equal to that
      new id and applyNumberFormat="1", the second is byte for byte the string
      "Harness runs" gives for it (P2 ruling 2), and count grows by two.
    
    For the worksheet, as specs/0011's P2 comparison does: the bytes outside
    sheetData identical, and every cell as the tuple (reference, s, t, formula
    presence, value text, has <v>) counted unchanged, changed, added and removed.
    The changed references must be exactly A when A exists and none when it does
    not, with A's t, formula presence and value text the input's and its s alone
    different; the added reference must be exactly (M + 1, 1) with s equal to X +
    1; and nothing is removed.
    
    It prints ONE line of counts and yes/no flags: no reference, no value, no
    text, no format code and no part name. With --parts it prints two part names
    on two lines (the sheet and the styles part, or nothing) for the log to
    compare with the runner's entry rows; the log never prints them.
    
    --plant <flag> makes one planted difference in the output before the
    comparison, chosen so that the named flag, and in general that flag alone,
    turns from yes to no: the control for every flag this comparison raises.
    """
    import posixpath
    import re
    import sys
    import xml.parsers.expat
    import zipfile
    
    MAIN = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/spreadsheetml/main")
    RELS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships"
    ATTR = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/officeDocument/relationships")
    
    
    def rels_name(part):
        d, base = posixpath.split(part)
        return posixpath.join(d, "_rels", base + ".rels") if base else "_rels/.rels"
    
    
    def rels_of(z, part):
        d = posixpath.dirname(part)
        name = rels_name(part)
        out = []
        if name not in z.namelist():
            return out
        found = []
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            if tag == RELS + " Relationship" and attrs.get("TargetMode") != "External":
                found.append(attrs)
        p = xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate(namespace_separator=" ")
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.Parse(z.read(name), True)
        for a in found:
            target = a.get("Target", "")
            resolved = (target[1:] if target.startswith("/")
                        else posixpath.normpath(posixpath.join(d, target)))
            out.append((a.get("Id"), a.get("Type", ""), resolved))
        return out
    
    
    def workbook_of(z):
        office = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, "") if ty.endswith("/officeDocument")]
        return office[0] if len(office) == 1 else None
    
    
    def worksheets(z, workbook):
        by_id = {i: (ty, t) for (i, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook)}
        order = []
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            ns, _, local = tag.rpartition(" ")
            if ns in MAIN and local == "sheet":
                for a in ATTR:
                    if a + " id" in attrs:
                        order.append(attrs[a + " id"])
        p = xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate(namespace_separator=" ")
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.Parse(z.read(workbook), True)
        out = []
        for rid in order:
            ty, target = by_id.get(rid, ("", None))
            if ty.endswith("/worksheet") and target in z.namelist():
                out.append(target)
        return out
    
    
    def chain_of(z, workbook):
        chains = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook) if ty.endswith("/calcChain")]
        return chains[0] if chains else None
    
    
    def cells(data):
        """{reference: tuple}, the document order, the <row> count, and the
        first cell with a normal formula."""
        out = {}
        order = []
        stack = []
        state = {"cell": None, "text": None, "rows": 0, "normal": None}
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            ns, _, local = tag.rpartition(" ")
            local = local if ns in MAIN else None
            stack.append(local)
            if local == "row" and stack[-2:-1] == ["sheetData"]:
                state["rows"] += 1
            if local == "c" and stack[-2:-1] == ["row"] and stack[-3:-2] == ["sheetData"]:
                state["cell"] = {"r": attrs.get("r"), "s": attrs.get("s"),
                                 "t": attrs.get("t"), "f": False, "normal": False,
                                 "v": None, "is": None}
            elif state["cell"] is not None:
                if local == "f" and stack[-2:-1] == ["c"]:
                    state["cell"]["f"] = True
                    state["cell"]["normal"] = attrs.get("t", "normal") == "normal"
                elif local == "v" and stack[-2:-1] == ["c"]:
                    state["text"] = "v"
                    state["cell"]["v"] = ""
                elif local == "is" and stack[-2:-1] == ["c"]:
                    state["cell"]["is"] = ""
                elif local == "t" and "is" in stack:
                    state["text"] = "is"
    
        def end(tag):
            local = stack.pop()
            if local in ("v", "t"):
                state["text"] = None
            if local == "c" and state["cell"] is not None and stack[-1:] == ["row"]:
                c = state["cell"]
                value = c["v"] if c["v"] is not None else c["is"]
                out[c["r"]] = (c["r"], c["s"], c["t"], c["f"], value, c["v"] is not None)
                order.append(c["r"])
                if c["normal"] and state["normal"] is None:
                    state["normal"] = c["r"]
                state["cell"] = None
    
        def chars(text):
            if state["cell"] is not None and state["text"] is not None:
                state["cell"][state["text"]] += text
    
        p = xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate(namespace_separator=" ")
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.EndElementHandler = end
        p.CharacterDataHandler = chars
        p.buffer_text = True
        p.Parse(data, True)
        return out, order, state["rows"], state["normal"]
    
    
    def bounds(data):
        """(prefix end, end tag start or None for <sheetData/>, element end)."""
        start = re.search(rb"<([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?sheetData[\s/>]", data)
        if start is None:
            return None
        close = data.find(b">", start.start())
        if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
            return start.start(), None, close + 1
        ends = list(re.finditer(rb"</([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?sheetData\s*>", data))
        if not ends:
            return None
        return start.start(), ends[-1].start(), ends[-1].end()
    
    
    
    
    def styles_of(z, workbook):
        """The styles part the workbook names, or None."""
        parts = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook) if ty.endswith("/styles")]
        return parts[0] if parts and parts[0] in z.namelist() else None
    
    
    def container(data, name):
        """The spans of one root child: (start of its start tag, start of its
        children, end of its children, end of the element), or None when the part
        has no such element. An empty element has equal child bounds."""
        start = re.search(rb"<([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?" + name + rb"[\s/>]", data)
        if start is None:
            return None
        close = data.find(b">", start.start())
        if close < 0:
            return None
        if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
            return start.start(), close + 1, close + 1, close + 1
        ends = list(re.finditer(rb"</([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?" + name + rb"\s*>", data))
        if not ends:
            return None
        return start.start(), close + 1, ends[-1].start(), ends[-1].end()
    
    
    def count_attribute(data, span):
        """The count attribute of the start tag at span, as an int, or None."""
        tag = data[span[0]:span[1]]
        found = re.search(rb"\scount\s*=\s*(\"[^\"]*\"|'[^']*')", tag)
        if found is None:
            return None
        try:
            return int(found.group(1)[1:-1])
        except ValueError:
            return None
    
    
    def elements(data):
        """The (name, attributes, bytes) of every top-level element in data,
        which is a container's children."""
        out = []
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            ns, _, local = tag.rpartition(" ")
            out.append((local if ns in MAIN else None, attrs))
        p = xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate(namespace_separator=" ")
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.Parse(b"<r xmlns='" + MAIN[0].encode() + b"'>" + data + b"</r>", True)
        return out[1:]
    
    
    def num_fmt_ids(data):
        """The numFmtId of every numFmt among a numFmts container's children."""
        out = []
        for (local, attrs) in elements(data):
            if local == "numFmt" and "numFmtId" in attrs:
                try:
                    out.append(int(attrs["numFmtId"]))
                except ValueError:
                    pass
        return out
    
    
    def top_level(data):
        """The children's bytes cut into one span per top-level element, so an
        addition can be counted and read without a parser that keeps offsets."""
        spans = []
        depth = 0
        at = 0
        i = 0
        while i < len(data):
            if data[i:i + 1] == b"<" and data[i + 1:i + 2] not in (b"/", b"!", b"?"):
                if depth == 0:
                    at = i
                close = data.find(b">", i)
                if close < 0:
                    break
                empty = data[close - 1:close] == b"/"
                if empty:
                    if depth == 0:
                        spans.append((at, close + 1))
                else:
                    depth += 1
                i = close + 1
                continue
            if data[i:i + 2] == b"</":
                close = data.find(b">", i)
                if close < 0:
                    break
                depth -= 1
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((at, close + 1))
                i = close + 1
                continue
            i += 1
        return spans
    
    
    def col_of(reference):
        """The 1-based column of an A1 reference."""
        letters = re.match(r"[A-Za-z]+", reference or "")
        if letters is None:
            return 0
        n = 0
        for ch in letters.group(0).upper():
            n = n * 26 + (ord(ch) - 64)
        return n
    
    
    def row_of(reference):
        digits = re.search(r"\d+", reference or "")
        return int(digits.group(0)) if digits else 0
    
    
    def a1(row, col):
        name = ""
        while col > 0:
            col, rest = divmod(col - 1, 26)
            name = chr(65 + rest) + name
        return "%s%d" % (name, row)
    
    
    def sampled(data):
        """A (the first cell of a sampled kind with a value and no formula), M
        (the largest row among the cells) and the cell count of one sheet."""
        found, order, _, _ = cells(data)
        a = None
        top = 0
        for ref in order:
            (_, _, t, formula, value, has_v) = found[ref]
            top = max(top, row_of(ref))
            candidate = (t in (None, "n", "s") and has_v and value is not None
                         and value != "" and not formula)
            if candidate and a is None:
                a = ref
        return a, top, found, order
    
    
    def pick(z):
        """The workbook, its first worksheet, its styles part, A and M."""
        workbook = workbook_of(z)
        if workbook is None:
            return None, None, None, None, 0
        sheets = worksheets(z, workbook)
        part = sheets[0] if sheets else None
        styles = styles_of(z, workbook)
        if part is None:
            return workbook, None, styles, None, 0
        a, top, _, _ = sampled(z.read(part))
        return workbook, part, styles, a, top
    
    
    PLANTS = (
        "head_same", "mid_same", "tail_same", "fmts_prefix", "fmt_added",
        "fmt_id_ok", "fmt_count_grew", "xfs_prefix", "xfs_added", "coded_xf_ok",
        "dated_xf_ok", "xf_count_grew", "ws_prefix_same", "ws_suffix_same",
        "changed_as_styled", "added_as_edited", "nothing_removed",
        # Not a flag: a second plant for dated_xf_ok that keeps every attribute
        # and value and only reorders them, which byte equality must catch
        # (P2 ruling 2).
        "dated_xf_order",
    )
    
    
    def plant_styles(data, flag, ids, fmts_in):
        """The planted difference for a styles-part flag, and whether it applied.
    
        A plant that cannot falsify its flag on this pair does not apply, and
        says so rather than leaving a flag that passes for want of a difference:
        an input with no numFmts of its own makes the prefix flag vacuous, since
        every byte string starts with an empty one.
        """
        fmts = container(data, b"numFmts")
        xfs = container(data, b"cellXfs")
        if flag == "head_same":
            # Just before the first of the two containers, which is where the
            # head span ends: a comment there lands in the head and nowhere else.
            at = fmts[0] if fmts is not None else xfs[0]
            return data[:at] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[at:], True
        if flag == "mid_same" and fmts is not None:
            return data[:fmts[3]] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[fmts[3]:], True
        if flag == "tail_same":
            return data[:xfs[3]] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[xfs[3]:], True
        if flag == "fmts_prefix" and fmts is not None and fmts_in:
            spans = top_level(data[fmts[1]:fmts[2]])
            if spans:
                at = fmts[1] + spans[0][0]
                return data[:at] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[at:], True
        if flag == "fmt_added" and fmts is not None:
            return data[:fmts[2]] + b'<numFmt numFmtId="199" formatCode="0.0000"/>' + data[fmts[2]:], True
        if flag == "fmt_id_ok" and fmts is not None:
            spans = top_level(data[fmts[1]:fmts[2]])
            if spans:
                last = data[fmts[1] + spans[-1][0]:fmts[1] + spans[-1][1]]
                other = re.sub(rb'numFmtId\s*=\s*"\d+"', b'numFmtId="199"', last, count=1)
                return data[:fmts[1] + spans[-1][0]] + other + data[fmts[1] + spans[-1][1]:], True
        if flag == "fmt_count_grew" and fmts is not None:
            tag = data[fmts[0]:fmts[1]]
            # Zero is never the count a growing container should carry, whatever
            # the input held, so this plant is wrong on every pair.
            return data[:fmts[0]] + re.sub(rb'count\s*=\s*"\d+"', b'count="0"', tag, count=1) \
                + data[fmts[1]:], True
        if flag == "xfs_prefix":
            spans = top_level(data[xfs[1]:xfs[2]])
            if spans:
                at = xfs[1] + spans[0][0]
                return data[:at] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[at:], True
        if flag == "xfs_added":
            return data[:xfs[2]] + b"<xf/>" + data[xfs[2]:], True
        if flag in ("coded_xf_ok", "dated_xf_ok"):
            spans = top_level(data[xfs[1]:xfs[2]])
            which = -2 if flag == "coded_xf_ok" else -1
            if len(spans) >= 2:
                at = xfs[1] + spans[which][0]
                to = xfs[1] + spans[which][1]
                return data[:at] + b'<xf numFmtId="0"/>' + data[to:], True
        if flag == "dated_xf_order":
            spans = top_level(data[xfs[1]:xfs[2]])
            if len(spans) >= 2:
                at = xfs[1] + spans[-1][0]
                to = xfs[1] + spans[-1][1]
                return data[:at] + DATED_XF_REORDERED + data[to:], True
        if flag == "xf_count_grew":
            tag = data[xfs[0]:xfs[1]]
            return data[:xfs[0]] + re.sub(rb'count\s*=\s*"\d+"', b'count="0"', tag, count=1) \
                + data[xfs[1]:], True
        return data, False
    
    
    def cell_spans(data, upto):
        """One span per top-level <c> element inside sheetData."""
        spans = []
        for hit in re.finditer(rb"<([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?c[\s/>]", data[:upto]):
            at = hit.start()
            close = data.find(b">", at)
            if close < 0:
                break
            if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
                spans.append((at, close + 1))
                continue
            end = re.compile(rb"</([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?c\s*>").search(data, close)
            if end is None:
                break
            spans.append((at, end.end()))
        return spans
    
    
    def reference_of(span_bytes):
        hit = re.search(rb'\sr\s*=\s*"([^"]*)"', span_bytes)
        return hit.group(1).decode("ascii", "replace") if hit else ""
    
    
    def plant_sheet(data, flag, a, added):  # noqa: C901
        """The planted difference for a worksheet flag, or the bytes unchanged.
    
        A cell the edit itself touched is never the target: a plant on A or on
        the added cell would leave the flag it is meant to turn as it was.
        """
        span = bounds(data)
        if span is None:
            return data, False
        rows = list(re.finditer(rb"<([A-Za-z_][\w.-]*:)?row[\s/>]", data))
        prefix = rows[-1].group(1) if rows and rows[-1].group(1) else b""
        at = span[1] if span[1] is not None else span[2]
        if flag == "ws_prefix_same":
            return data[:span[0]] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[span[0]:], True
        if flag == "ws_suffix_same":
            return data[:span[2]] + b"<!-- planted -->" + data[span[2]:], True
        if flag == "added_as_edited":
            # Inside the last row, not beside it: a <c> that is not a row's child
            # is no cell, so a plant there would be read as no difference at all.
            cell = (b"<" + prefix + b'c r="ZZ999998" s="0"><' + prefix + b"v>0</"
                    + prefix + b"v></" + prefix + b"c>")
            close = data.rfind(b"</" + prefix + b"row>", 0, at)
            if close < 0:
                row = (b"<" + prefix + b'row r="999998">' + cell + b"</" + prefix + b"row>")
                return data[:at] + row + data[at:], True
            return data[:close] + cell + data[close:], True
        if flag in ("changed_as_styled", "nothing_removed"):
            spans = [s for s in cell_spans(data, at)
                     if reference_of(data[s[0]:s[1]]) not in (a, added)]
            if not spans:
                return data, False
            start, end = spans[-1]
            if flag == "nothing_removed":
                return data[:start] + data[end:], True
            # One more changed cell: its `s` is set to a value it did not carry,
            # which is exactly what the flag says only A may have.
            cell = data[start:end]
            if re.search(rb'\ss\s*=\s*"[^"]*"', cell):
                other = re.sub(rb'\ss\s*=\s*"[^"]*"', b' s="0"', cell, count=1)
                if other == cell:
                    other = re.sub(rb'\ss\s*=\s*"[^"]*"', b' s="1"', cell, count=1)
            else:
                close = cell.find(b">")
                cut = close - 1 if cell[close - 1:close] == b"/" else close
                other = cell[:cut] + b' s="0"' + cell[cut:]
            if other == cell:
                return data, False
            return data[:start] + other + data[end:], True
        return data, False
    
    
    # The second added xf, exactly as "Harness runs" P2 writes it (P2 ruling 2).
    DATED_XF = (b'<xf numFmtId="14" fontId="0" fillId="0" borderId="0" xfId="0" '
                b'applyNumberFormat="1"/>')
    # The same attributes and values in another order: the reorder plant.
    DATED_XF_REORDERED = (b'<xf fontId="0" numFmtId="14" fillId="0" borderId="0" xfId="0" '
                          b'applyNumberFormat="1"/>')
    
    
    def creation_point(data, fallback):
        """Where a numFmts the part does not have is created: the start of the
        first of fonts, fills, borders, cellStyleXfs and cellXfs that the part
        holds, whichever comes first in the part's own order."""
        starts = []
        for name in (b"fonts", b"fills", b"borders", b"cellStyleXfs", b"cellXfs"):
            span = container(data, name)
            if span is not None:
                starts.append(span[0])
        return min(starts) if starts else fallback
    
    
    def styles_flags(din, dout, expect_id):
        """Every styles-part flag, by bytes, and the two counts the line carries.
    
        A part with no numFmts of its own is the case the spec names: the head
        then runs to <cellXfs and the created container is the addition itself.
        """
        out = {}
        fin, fout = container(din, b"numFmts"), container(dout, b"numFmts")
        xin, xout = container(din, b"cellXfs"), container(dout, b"cellXfs")
        if xin is None or xout is None or fout is None:
            return None, 0, 0
        # Where a created numFmts goes: before the first of the five the part
        # holds, in the part's own order (specs/0012, P1 verification ruling 5).
        # For a part that has one already the head simply ends at it.
        cut = fin[0] if fin is not None else creation_point(din, xin[0])
        out["head_same"] = din[:cut] == dout[:fout[0]]
        out["mid_same"] = din[fin[3] if fin is not None else cut:xin[0]] \
            == dout[fout[3]:xout[0]]
        out["tail_same"] = din[xin[3]:] == dout[xout[3]:]
    
        fmts_in = din[fin[1]:fin[2]] if fin is not None else b""
        fmts_out = dout[fout[1]:fout[2]]
        out["fmts_prefix"] = fmts_out.startswith(fmts_in)
        rest = top_level(fmts_out[len(fmts_in):])
        added_fmts = [fmts_out[len(fmts_in):][s[0]:s[1]] for s in rest]
        out["fmt_added"] = len(added_fmts) == 1 and num_fmt_ids(added_fmts[0]) != []
        ids = num_fmt_ids(added_fmts[0]) if out["fmt_added"] else []
        out["fmt_id_ok"] = ids == [expect_id]
        count_in = count_attribute(din, fin) if fin is not None else 0
        count_out = count_attribute(dout, fout)
        fmts_before = len(num_fmt_ids(fmts_in))
        fmts_after = len(num_fmt_ids(fmts_out))
        # The library writes the container's count from its CHILDREN plus the
        # additions, not from whatever the input's attribute said, so that is
        # what this flag holds it to: the output's count is its own children's
        # number, and that number is one more than the input's. Whether the
        # input's own attribute agreed with its children is a property of the
        # INPUT and is reported beside the flag rather than folded into it.
        out["fmt_count_grew"] = count_out is not None and count_out == fmts_after \
            and fmts_after == fmts_before + 1
        out["_fmt_count_in_matched"] = (count_in or 0) == fmts_before
    
        xfs_in = din[xin[1]:xin[2]]
        xfs_out = dout[xout[1]:xout[2]]
        out["xfs_prefix"] = xfs_out.startswith(xfs_in)
        spans = top_level(xfs_out[len(xfs_in):])
        added_xfs = [xfs_out[len(xfs_in):][s[0]:s[1]] for s in spans]
        out["xfs_added"] = len(added_xfs) == 2
        coded = added_xfs[0] if out["xfs_added"] else b""
        dated = added_xfs[1] if out["xfs_added"] else b""
        out["coded_xf_ok"] = (b'numFmtId="%d"' % expect_id) in coded \
            and b'applyNumberFormat="1"' in coded
        out["dated_xf_ok"] = dated == DATED_XF
        xfs_count_in = count_attribute(din, xin)
        xfs_count_out = count_attribute(dout, xout)
        xfs_in_n = len(top_level(xfs_in))
        xfs_out_n = len(top_level(xfs_out))
        out["xf_count_grew"] = xfs_count_out is not None and xfs_count_out == xfs_out_n \
            and xfs_out_n == xfs_in_n + 2
        out["_xf_count_in_matched"] = xfs_count_in == xfs_in_n
        return out, xfs_in_n, fmts_after - fmts_before
    
    
    def main():
        zin = zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[1])
        workbook, part, styles, a, top = pick(zin)
        if sys.argv[2:3] == ["--parts"]:
            print(part or "")
            print(styles or "")
            return
        zout = zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[2])
        plant = None
        if "--plant" in sys.argv[3:]:
            plant = sys.argv[sys.argv.index("--plant") + 1]
            if plant not in PLANTS:
                print("error=unknown-plant")
                return
        yn = lambda v: "yes" if v else "no"
        if part is None or styles is None:
            print("found=0")
            return
        added = a1(top + 1, 1)
        sin, sout = zin.read(styles), zout.read(styles)
        din, dout = zin.read(part), zout.read(part)
        ids = num_fmt_ids(sin[container(sin, b"numFmts")[1]:container(sin, b"numFmts")[2]]) \
            if container(sin, b"numFmts") is not None else []
        expect_id = max(164, max(ids) + 1) if ids else 164
        planted = True
        if plant is not None:
            fmts_in = container(sin, b"numFmts") is not None
            sout, in_styles = plant_styles(sout, plant, ids, fmts_in)
            dout, in_sheet = plant_sheet(dout, plant, a, added)
            planted = in_styles or in_sheet
    
        flags, xfs_before, formats_added = styles_flags(sin, sout, expect_id)
        if flags is None:
            print("error=no-container")
            return
        out_xfs = container(sout, b"cellXfs")
        xfs_after = len(top_level(sout[out_xfs[1]:out_xfs[2]]))
    
        bi, bo = bounds(din), bounds(dout)
        if bi is None or bo is None:
            print("error=no-sheetData")
            return
        ws_prefix_same = din[:bi[0]] == dout[:bo[0]]
        if bi[1] is not None and bo[1] is not None:
            ws_suffix_same = din[bi[1]:] == dout[bo[1]:]
        else:
            ws_suffix_same = din[bi[2]:] == dout[bo[2]:]
        cin, _, _, _ = cells(din)
        cout, _, _, _ = cells(dout)
        unchanged = changed = removed = 0
        changed_refs = set()
        for ref, tup in cin.items():
            if ref not in cout:
                removed += 1
            elif cout[ref] == tup:
                unchanged += 1
            else:
                changed += 1
                changed_refs.add(ref)
        added_refs = set(cout) - set(cin)
        styled = 1 if a is not None else 0
        if a is not None and a in cout and a in cin:
            # A's `s` alone differs: its t, formula presence and value are the
            # input's, and its new `s` is the first of the two added formats.
            a_kept = cout[a][2:] == cin[a][2:] and cout[a][1] != cin[a][1] \
                and cout[a][1] == str(xfs_before)
        else:
            a_kept = a is None
        changed_as_styled = changed == styled and changed_refs == ({a} if a else set()) \
            and a_kept
        added_as_edited = added_refs == {added} and added in cout \
            and cout[added][1] == str(xfs_before + 1) \
            and col_of(added) == 1 and row_of(added) == top + 1
        print(" ".join([
            "found=1", "planted=%s" % yn(planted), "styled=%d" % styled,
            "xfs_before=%d" % xfs_before,
            "xfs_after=%d" % xfs_after,
            "formats_added=%d" % formats_added,
            "cells_in=%d" % len(cin), "cells_out=%d" % len(cout),
            "unchanged=%d" % unchanged, "changed=%d" % changed,
            "added=%d" % len(added_refs), "removed=%d" % removed,
        ] + ["%s=%s" % (name, yn(flags[name])) for name in (
            "head_same", "mid_same", "tail_same", "fmts_prefix", "fmt_added",
            "fmt_id_ok", "fmt_count_grew", "xfs_prefix", "xfs_added",
            "coded_xf_ok", "dated_xf_ok", "xf_count_grew")]
          + ["fmt_count_in_matched=%s" % yn(flags["_fmt_count_in_matched"]),
             "xf_count_in_matched=%s" % yn(flags["_xf_count_in_matched"]),
             "ws_prefix_same=%s" % yn(ws_prefix_same),
             "ws_suffix_same=%s" % yn(ws_suffix_same),
             "changed_as_styled=%s" % yn(changed_as_styled),
             "added_as_edited=%s" % yn(added_as_edited),
             "nothing_removed=%s" % yn(removed == 0)]))
    
    
    main()

